@title EPISODE 13 • HOLLOWAY'S LINE
@bg track_stadium_morning
Monday. Holloway posts the conference lineup. London's 10K is gone. Alana's in it. So is Priya.
@show london
London: Coach. My name isn't on the 10K.
Holloway: I'm aware. I wrote it.
London: I'm faster than Priya.
Holloway: You're faster than everybody. You also skipped two recovery runs and talked back in front of freshmen. Speed isn't the only thing I coach.
> [Bitchy] "My dad paid for this track, you know." -> h1
> [Sweet] "...What do I have to do to earn it back?" -> h2
> [Bold] "Then put me in the 5K and watch." -> h3
> [Bad] Storm off and skip practice. -> h4
*h1
@add Coach_Respect -4
@add Team_Reputation -3
The whole track goes silent. Holloway doesn't blink.
Holloway: He paid for the lights, Sterling. I decide who runs under them. Go home.
@jump h_done
*h2
@add Coach_Respect 4
Holloway: (surprised, then not) Two weeks of perfect practice. No lip. And you help Priya with her pacing.
London: Priya?
Holloway: Priya.
@jump h_done
*h3
@add Coach_Respect 2
@add London_Confidence 2
Holloway: (half a smile) Now THAT'S the right kind of mouthy. 5K's yours. Don't make me regret it.
@jump h_done
*h4
@add Coach_Respect -3
@add Diggy_Trust -1
Diggy finds you at the coffee shop two hours later.
Diggy: You can't run from stuff that's on a track, Sterling. It goes in a circle.
*h_done
@show priya
Priya: (stretching next to you) So. Coach says you're supposed to help me.
London: Apparently.
Priya: For the record, I'd rather lose than be your charity project.
London: For the record, I'd rather be anywhere than here. Let's both be miserable and fast.
Priya laughs. It's the start of something.
@add Priya_Friendship 1
